.00)."],"better":"88.Kh6 prepares g6 and Ra6. Engine line: 88…a3 89.g6 a2 90.Ra6 Re2 91.g7 (0.00)."},{"ply":176,"name":"88…Rxf7","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"88…Rxf7! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the rook on f7.","The next best move, 88…a3, would drop Black's winning chances from 94% to 53% (−0.35).","88…Rxf7 trades rooks.","Trades rooks: trading pieces when ahead brings the win closer.","The rook on f7 can be taken by the king.","White answers 89.Kxf7, taking back, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on a3."]},{"ply":178,"name":"89…a3","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"89…a3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Pushes the passed pawn to a3, close to promotion.","The next best move, 89…c5, would drop Black's winning chances from 94% to 71% (−2.48).","89…a3 pushes the passed pawn to a3.","White answers 90.g6, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on a2.","After 90.g6 a2 91.g7 a1=Q 92.g8=Q Qa2+, the pawn promotes on a1 and the pawn promotes on g8 (−7.24)."]},{"ply":180,"name":"90…a2","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"90…a2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Pushes the passed pawn to a2, close to promotion.","The next best move, 90…c6, would drop Black's winning chances from 92% to 59% (−0.99).","90…a2 pushes the passed pawn to a2.","White answers 91.g7.","After 91.g7 a1=R 92.g8=Q Rf1+ 93.Kg7 Rg1+, the pawn promotes on a1, the pawn promotes on g8 and Black is a piece and a pawn down (−6.72)."]}],"opening":{"name":"Italian Game: Two Knights Defense, Modern Bishop's Opening","eco":"C55","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 6.a4: 11 moves in all, 6 by White and 5 by Black.","Theory runs out after 6.a4: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}